    "notes": "AlPO$_{4}$-5",
    "comments": "AlPO$_{4}$ can be found in a wide variety of structures (Wilson, 1982).  The variants included in the Encyclopedia can be found on the \\href{current_web_home_dir/Tutorials/SiO2_AlPO4}{silica/AlPO$_{4}$ page}. \n Ordered AlPO$_{4}$-5 can have the metallic atoms \\href{current_web_home_dir/AB4C_hP72_184_d_4d_d-001}{ordered, space group $P6cc$ \\#186} (Klapp, 184), although (Ruiz-Salvador, 1996) find it in \\href{current_web_home_dir/AB4C_hP72_168_2d_8d_2d-001}{space group $P6$ \\#168}, and (Mora, 1996) find it in \\href{current_web_home_dir/AB4C_oP144_27_6e_24e_6e-001}{space group $Pcc2$ \\#27} (this structure). \n It may also have \\href{current_web_home_dir/AB2_hP72_192_m_j2kl-001}{disordered aluminum/phosphorous sites, space group $P6/mcc$ \\#192} (Richardson, 1987)."
